---
import PageLayout from "@layouts/PageLayout.astro"
---
<PageLayout title="Ocean ecosystem" description="Explore a browser adaptation of a collaborative Processing food-chain simulation.">
  <div class="ocean-page">
    <a href="/projects/early-ocean-simulation/" class="back">← Original project & credits</a>
    <p class="eyebrow">Interactive adaptation · 2026</p>
    <h1>A living ocean.<br /><span>A thousand interactions.</span></h1>
    <p class="intro">Plant a food source. Add a hunter. Watch simple rules ripple through an ecosystem.</p>
    <section class="ocean-shell" aria-label="Ocean ecosystem simulation">
      <div class="toolbar">
        <div><span class="dot"></span> <strong>Ocean lab</strong> <span class="running" data-state>Paused</span></div>
        <div class="actions"><button id="play" type="button">Start simulation</button><button id="reset" type="button">Reset</button></div>
      </div>
      <p id="benchmark" hidden aria-live="off">Press Start for a ten-second benchmark sample.</p>
      <div class="viewport">
        <canvas id="ocean" width="960" height="540" aria-label="Animated ocean food chain. Use the controls below to add organisms and change the current." role="img"></canvas>
        <p class="canvas-note">Algae → Prey → Predator → Apex predator</p>
      </div>
      <div class="population" aria-label="Current population">
        <div><i style="--species:#69d59b"></i>Algae <strong data-count="algae">378</strong></div>
        <div><i style="--species:#7dd9ef"></i>Prey <strong data-count="prey">196</strong></div>
        <div><i style="--species:#ffbd7b"></i>Predators <strong data-count="predator">35</strong></div>
        <div><i style="--species:#e5a8ef"></i>Apex <strong data-count="apex">14</strong></div>
      </div>
      <div class="controls">
        <fieldset><legend>Add life</legend><p>Use a button, or choose a species and tap the ocean.</p><div class="add-buttons"><button data-add="algae">+ Algae</button><button data-add="prey">+ Prey</button><button data-add="predator">+ Predator</button><button data-add="apex">+ Apex</button></div><label for="batch">Add at once <select id="batch"><option value="1">1 organism</option><option value="10" selected>10 organisms</option><option value="30">30 organisms</option></select></label><label for="species">Tap to place <select id="species"><option value="algae">Algae</option><option value="prey">Prey</option><option value="predator">Predator</option><option value="apex">Apex predator</option></select></label></fieldset>
        <fieldset><legend>See the invisible</legend><label><input id="flow" type="checkbox" /> Show ocean currents</label><label><input id="perception" type="checkbox" /> Show perception ranges (24 sampled)</label><label for="current">Current strength <output id="current-value">0.55</output></label><input id="current" type="range" min="0" max="1.5" step="0.05" value="0.55" /><p id="performance" aria-live="off">Rendering starts when you press Start.</p></fieldset>
        <fieldset><legend>Run an experiment</legend><label for="density">Ecosystem preset <select id="density"><option value="3">Coastal · 267 organisms</option><option value="7" selected>Reef · 623 organisms</option><option value="12">Open ocean · 1,068 organisms</option></select></label><label for="seed">World seed <input id="seed" type="number" min="0" max="999999" step="1" value="42" /></label><p>Reset applies the preset and seed. Worlds can grow to 2,400 organisms. Choose Coastal if your device needs a lighter world.</p><p id="summary" role="status" aria-live="polite">623 organisms · Paused · 0 seconds</p></fieldset>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="explanation"><section><h2>Every fish follows a few rules.</h2><p>Prey seek algae and flee hunters. Predators seek prey, while apex predators hunt both. Nearby fish separate, align, and move together. Feeding replenishes energy; enough energy allows reproduction.</p></section><section><h2>Change one thing. Observe.</h2><p>Add predators, switch off the current, or plant more algae. Populations can collapse. Reset gives you a fresh start. Dense worlds take more work per frame; choose Coastal for lighter devices. This is a simplified educational model, not a scientifically calibrated ocean.</p></section></div>
    <p class="credits">A new browser interpretation of the Processing project by <strong>Andrés Brenes Maleaño, Axel Fernández Jiménez, and Bryand Flores Medina</strong>. Original sprites and desktop code are not bundled. <a href="https://github.com/axelfj/Simulacion-de-Jerarquia-Alimenticia-en-el-Oceano" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Original source ↗</a> · <a href="https://github.com/axelfj/portfolio/tree/main/src/lib/ocean.ts" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Browser simulation source ↗</a></p>
    <noscript><p>The interactive simulation requires JavaScript. The original project description and source links remain available above.</p></noscript>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
<script>
  import { Ocean, LIMIT, type Species, type Agent } from "../../lib/ocean"
  const canvas = document.querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>("#ocean")!
  const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d")!
  const play = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("#play")!
  const reset = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("#reset")!
  const flow = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("#flow")!
  const perception = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("#perception")!
  const current = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("#current")!
  const seed = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("#seed")!
  const select = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("#species")!
  const summary = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#summary")!
  const density = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("#density")!
  const batch = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("#batch")!
  const performanceLabel = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#performance")!
  const countLabels = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-count]")]
  const stateLabel = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-state]")!
  const benchmark = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#benchmark")!
  const benchmarkEnabled = new URLSearchParams(location.search).get("benchmark") === "1"
  benchmark.hidden = !benchmarkEnabled
  let benchmarkStarted = 0, benchmarkComplete = false
  let benchmarkWork: number[] = []
  function resetBenchmark() {
    benchmarkStarted = 0; benchmarkComplete = false; benchmarkWork = []
    for (const key of ["fps", "averageMs", "p95Ms", "population", "seconds"]) delete benchmark.dataset[key]
    benchmark.textContent = "Keep the ocean visible for a ten-second benchmark sample."
  }
  let world = new Ocean(42, LIMIT, 7), playing = false, last = 0, accumulated = 0, lastReport = -1, animation = 0, capped = false
  let frames = 0, workTime = 0, sampleStarted = 0, droppedTime = 0
  let inView = true
  const STEP = 1 / 30
  const previous = new WeakMap<Agent, { x: number; y: number }>()
  const colors = { algae: "#69d59b", prey: "#7dd9ef", predator: "#ffbd7b", apex: "#e5a8ef" }
  function report(force = false) {
    if (!force && Math.floor(world.time / 2) === lastReport) return
    lastReport = Math.floor(world.time / 2)
    const counts = world.counts()
    countLabels.forEach(el => el.textContent = String(counts[el.dataset.count as Species]))
    summary.textContent = `${world.agents.length}/${LIMIT} organisms · ${playing ? "Running" : "Paused"} · ${Math.floor(world.time)} seconds${capped ? " · Population limit reached" : ""}`
    stateLabel.textContent = playing ? "Running" : "Paused"
  }
  // Static scenery is painted once. Sprite variants are also cached so drawing
  // more fish does not create hundreds of paths and canvas state changes.
  const background = document.createElement("canvas")
  background.width = 960; background.height = 540
  const bg = background.getContext("2d")!
  {
    const gradient = bg.createLinearGradient(0, 0, 0, 540)
    gradient.addColorStop(0, "#102f42"); gradient.addColorStop(1, "#061d29")
    bg.fillStyle = gradient; bg.fillRect(0, 0, 960, 540)
    // Diffuse surface light and a planted seabed.
    for (let x = -100; x < 1000; x += 170) {
      bg.fillStyle = "#9bdeed06"; bg.beginPath(); bg.moveTo(x, 0); bg.lineTo(x + 70, 0); bg.lineTo(x + 230, 540); bg.lineTo(x + 100, 540); bg.fill()
    }
    bg.fillStyle = "#12434b"; bg.beginPath(); bg.moveTo(0, 540)
    for (let x = 0; x <= 960; x += 12) bg.lineTo(x, 513 + Math.sin(x / 75) * 12)
    bg.lineTo(960, 540); bg.fill()
    for (let x = 16; x < 960; x += 31) {
      bg.strokeStyle = "#447c6b77"; bg.lineWidth = 3
      bg.beginPath(); bg.moveTo(x, 535); bg.quadraticCurveTo(x - 12, 510, x + 5, 480 + Math.sin(x) * 16); bg.stroke()
    }
  }
  const sprites = new Map<Species, HTMLCanvasElement[]>()
  for (const kind of ["algae", "prey", "predator", "apex"] as Species[]) {
    const variants: HTMLCanvasElement[] = []
    for (let direction = 0; direction < (kind === "algae" ? 1 : 48); direction++) {
      const sprite = document.createElement("canvas"); sprite.width = sprite.height = 48
      const paint = sprite.getContext("2d")!; paint.translate(24, 24)
      paint.rotate(direction / 48 * Math.PI * 2); paint.fillStyle = colors[kind]
      if (kind === "algae") {
        paint.beginPath(); paint.arc(0, 0, 3, 0, Math.PI * 2); paint.fill()
        paint.strokeStyle = "#69d59b55"; paint.beginPath(); paint.moveTo(0, 0); paint.lineTo(0, 8); paint.stroke()
      } else {
        const size = kind === "prey" ? 5 : kind === "predator" ? 8 : 11
        paint.beginPath(); paint.ellipse(0, 0, size, size * .5, 0, 0, Math.PI * 2); paint.fill()
        paint.beginPath(); paint.moveTo(-size + 1, 0); paint.lineTo(-size * 1.7, -size * .5); paint.lineTo(-size * 1.7, size * .5); paint.fill()
        paint.fillStyle = "#092533"; paint.beginPath(); paint.arc(size * .5, -1, 1.1, 0, Math.PI * 2); paint.fill()
      }
      variants.push(sprite)
    }
    sprites.set(kind, variants)
  }
  function draw() {
    ctx.drawImage(background, 0, 0)
    if (flow.checked) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = "#7dd9ef55"
      for (let x = 30; x < 960; x += 60) for (let y = 30; y < 540; y += 60) {
        const f = world.flow(x, y)
        ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(x, y); ctx.lineTo(x + f.x * 2, y + f.y * 2); ctx.stroke()
        ctx.fillStyle = "#7dd9ef66"; ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(x + f.x * 2, y + f.y * 2, 1.5, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill()
      }
    }
    let ranges = 0
    for (const a of world.agents) {
      const old = playing ? previous.get(a) : undefined
      const alpha = Math.min(1, accumulated / STEP)
      const x = old ? old.x + (a.x - old.x) * alpha : a.x
      const y = old ? old.y + (a.y - old.y) * alpha : a.y
      if (perception.checked && a.kind !== "algae" && ranges++ < 24) { ctx.strokeStyle = colors[a.kind] + "20"; ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(x, y, a.kind === "prey" ? 95 : a.kind === "predator" ? 145 : 170, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.stroke() }
      const direction = a.kind === "algae" ? 0 : Math.round((Math.atan2(a.vy, a.vx) + Math.PI * 2) / (Math.PI * 2) * 48) % 48
      ctx.drawImage(sprites.get(a.kind)![direction], x - 24, y - 24)
    }
  }
  function tick(now: number) {
    if (!playing) return
    const started = performance.now()
    const elapsed = (now - (last || now)) / 1000; last = now
    accumulated += Math.min(elapsed, .1); droppedTime += Math.max(0, elapsed - .1)
    let steps = 0
    while (accumulated >= STEP && steps < 3) {
      for (const a of world.agents) {
        const old = previous.get(a)
        if (old) { old.x = a.x; old.y = a.y }
        else previous.set(a, { x: a.x, y: a.y })
      }
      world.step(STEP); accumulated -= STEP; steps++
    }
    draw(); report()
    const frameWork = performance.now() - started
    workTime += frameWork; frames++
    if (benchmarkEnabled && !benchmarkComplete) {
      if (!benchmarkStarted) benchmarkStarted = now
      benchmarkWork.push(frameWork)
      const seconds = (now - benchmarkStarted) / 1000
      if (seconds >= 10) {
        const sorted = [...benchmarkWork].sort((a, b) => a - b)
        const fps = benchmarkWork.length / seconds
        const average = benchmarkWork.reduce((sum, value) => sum + value, 0) / benchmarkWork.length
        const p95 = sorted[Math.min(sorted.length - 1, Math.ceil(sorted.length * .95) - 1)]
        Object.assign(benchmark.dataset, { fps: fps.toFixed(2), averageMs: average.toFixed(3), p95Ms: p95.toFixed(3), population: String(world.agents.length), seconds: seconds.toFixed(3) })
        benchmark.textContent = `10-second sample: ${fps.toFixed(1)} rendered fps · ${average.toFixed(2)} ms average work · ${p95.toFixed(2)} ms p95 work · ${world.agents.length} organisms`
        benchmarkComplete = true
      }
    }
    if (now - sampleStarted >= 1000) {
      performanceLabel.textContent = `${Math.round(frames * 1000 / (now - sampleStarted))} rendered fps · ${(workTime / frames).toFixed(1)} ms work/frame${droppedTime > .1 ? " · Simulation slows under load" : ""}`
      frames = 0; workTime = 0; sampleStarted = now; droppedTime = 0
    }
    animation = requestAnimationFrame(tick)
  }
  function pause(reason = "Paused") { playing = false; cancelAnimationFrame(animation); accumulated = 0; play.textContent = "Resume simulation"; performanceLabel.textContent = reason; draw(); report(true) }
  play.addEventListener("click", () => { if (playing) pause(); else if (!document.hidden) {
    // Keyboard focus can reach Start while the canvas is outside a short viewport.
    // Bring the requested experiment into view rather than silently ignoring Start.
    if (!inView) canvas.scrollIntoView({ block: "center", behavior: "instant" })
    for (const a of world.agents) { const old = previous.get(a); if (old) { old.x = a.x; old.y = a.y } }
    resetBenchmark(); playing = true; last = 0; sampleStarted = performance.now(); frames = 0; workTime = 0; droppedTime = 0; play.textContent = "Pause"; report(true); animation = requestAnimationFrame(tick)
  } })
  reset.addEventListener("click", () => { pause(); resetBenchmark(); const value = Number(seed.value); const safe = Number.isFinite(value) ? Math.max(0, Math.min(999999, Math.floor(value))) : 42; seed.value = String(safe); world = new Ocean(safe, LIMIT, Number(density.value)); world.current = Number(current.value); capped = false; accumulated = 0; lastReport = -1; play.textContent = "Start simulation"; draw(); report(true) })
  function add(kind: Species, x?: number, y?: number) {
    capped = false
    for (let i = 0; i < Number(batch.value); i++) {
      const angle = i * 2.4, radius = Math.sqrt(i) * 5
      if (!world.add(kind, x === undefined ? undefined : x + Math.cos(angle) * radius, y === undefined ? undefined : y + Math.sin(angle) * radius)) { capped = true; break }
    }
    draw(); report(true)
  }
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-add]").forEach(button => button.addEventListener("click", () => add(button.dataset.add as Species)))
  canvas.addEventListener("pointerdown", event => { const rect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect(); add(select.value as Species, (event.clientX - rect.left) / rect.width * 960, (event.clientY - rect.top) / rect.height * 540) })
  current.addEventListener("input", () => { world.current = Number(current.value); document.querySelector("#current-value")!.textContent = current.value; draw() })
  flow.addEventListener("change", draw); perception.addEventListener("change", draw)
  const onVisibilityChange = () => { if (document.hidden && playing) pause("Paused while the tab is hidden") }
  document.addEventListener("visibilitychange", onVisibilityChange)
  const observer = new IntersectionObserver(entries => { inView = entries[0].isIntersecting; if (!inView && playing) pause("Paused while the ocean is offscreen") })
  observer.observe(canvas)
  document.addEventListener("astro:before-swap", () => { playing = false; cancelAnimationFrame(animation); observer.disconnect(); document.removeEventListener("visibilitychange", onVisibilityChange) }, { once: true })
  draw(); report(true)
</script>
<style>
  .ocean-page { max-width: 1120px; margin: 112px auto 80px; padding: 0 24px; }
  .back { font-size: .9rem; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  .eyebrow { margin-top: 44px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .15em; font-size: .75rem; color: var(--accent); }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 4rem); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -.045em; margin: 16px 0 24px; }
  h1 span { color: var(--accent); }
  .intro { max-width: 550px; font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .ocean-shell { border: 1px solid #36515d; border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; background: #0b2432; color: #e7f2f3; }
  .toolbar { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; padding: 16px 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid #284653; }
  .dot { display: inline-block; width: 8px; height: 8px; background: #9ab7e8; border-radius: 50%; margin-right: 7px; }
  .running { font-size: .75rem; margin-left: 12px; color: #b8cdd1; }
  #benchmark { padding: 12px 20px; font-size: .8rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; color: #b8cdd1; }
  .actions, .add-buttons { display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  button { background: #163b4a; color: #e7f2f3; border: 1px solid #50717c; border-radius: 5px; padding: 8px 12px; font-size: .85rem; cursor: pointer; }
  #play { background: #9ab7e8; color: #17243a; border-color: #9ab7e8; font-weight: 700; }
  button:hover { filter: brightness(1.15); }
  button:focus-visible, input:focus-visible, select:focus-visible, a:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #e8bd76; outline-offset: 4px; }
  .viewport { position: relative; }
  canvas { display: block; width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; cursor: crosshair; }
  .canvas-note { position: absolute; bottom: 10px; left: 16px; pointer-events: none; color: #b8d2d8; font-size: .7rem; background: #061d29cc; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 4px; }
  .population { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); border-top: 1px solid #284653; border-bottom: 1px solid #284653; }
  .population div { padding: 16px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font-size: .8rem; }
  .population strong { margin-left: auto; font-size: 1.4rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .population i { width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--species); flex-shrink: 0; }
  .controls { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr 1fr; gap: 28px; padding: 24px; }
  fieldset { min-width: 0; border: 0; padding: 0; }
  legend { font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  fieldset p { font-size: .8rem; color: #b8cdd1; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 14px; }
  label { display: block; font-size: .8rem; margin: 12px 0; }
  input[type="range"] { width: 100%; accent-color: #9ab7e8; }
  input[type="checkbox"] { accent-color: #9ab7e8; margin-right: 8px; }
  input[type="number"], select { display: block; width: 100%; background: #102f3d; border: 1px solid #50717c; color: #e7f2f3; padding: 8px; border-radius: 4px; margin-top: 8px; }
  output { float: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .explanation { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 48px; margin: 48px 0; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .explanation p, .credits { font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.8; }
  .credits { border-top: 1px solid #8a9d9f55; padding-top: 24px; }
  .credits a { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  @media(max-width: 700px) { .ocean-page { padding: 0 16px; margin-top: 96px; } .controls { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; padding: 20px; } .population { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } .population div { padding: 12px; } .explanation { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 28px; } .canvas-note { font-size: .55rem; bottom: 4px; left: 4px; } }
</style>
